Tobias Mummert <teergrube@phreaker.net> writes:
> according to the guidebook I have to wield a bow and some arrows readied
> in my quiver to fire an arrow with the 'f'-command.
> 
> Guess, I wield a bow, but I have an *empty* quiver and some arrows in my
> inventory, does the (t)hrow-command the same as the above mentioned
> (f)ire-command (damage and range)?

Yes. f)ire is just a shortcut for "t)hrow quivered item" (possibly
moving an item into the quiver first, depending on the setting of
the autoquiver option). There's no difference in the actual
execution of the action.

> If so, could I ready some stones or spears in my quiver, fire them with
> the (f) shortcut and use my bow and arrows by hitting (t)hrow without
> any damage or range penalty?

Certainly. (The stones will have the usual penalties for being thrown
by hand rather than slung, but they'd have that whether you used f or
t to throw them.)

